  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "The group CTP (Z) is finitely generated if and only if P is finite. If\nP = ∅, then it is isomorphic to the finitely presented (first) Higman–Thompson\ngroup (J. P. McDermott, see Remark 1.4 in S. Kohl, J. Group Theory, 20, no. 5 (2017),\n1025–1030). Is it always finitely presented if P is finite?                   S. Kohl",
